    <section class="section">
        <h2>What exists today</h2>

        <h3>Parachute Vault</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Self-hosted knowledge graph. Notes, tags, links, attachments.</li>
            <li><strong>9 MCP tools</strong> covering read, write, search, graph traversal, tag schemas, and vault info. Small surface, composes cleanly with any MCP client.</li>
            <li>REST API with full CRUD and full-text search.</li>
            <li>Bidirectional Obsidian import/export preserving frontmatter, tags, wikilinks.</li>
            <li><code>parachute vault</code> CLI: init, status, doctor, create/list/remove vaults, tokens, set-password, 2FA, backup with tiered retention, import/export, uninstall.</li>
            <li>Background daemon on macOS and Linux.</li>
            <li>Per-vault API keys; OAuth 2.1 + PKCE for interactive clients.</li>
            <li>Deployment recipes for Cloudflare Tunnel and Tailscale Funnel.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Parachute Daily</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Flutter app, iOS + Android + macOS.</li>
            <li>Three-tab UI: Reader / Capture / Vault.</li>
            <li>Voice capture with on-device transcription (offline-capable).</li>
            <li>Offline-first with a pending-write queue that flushes when reconnected.</li>
            <li>Multi-vault aware.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Parachute Pendant</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>PCB designed and printed in-house.</li>
            <li>3D-printed enclosure prototype.</li>
            <li>Audio-to-vault integration in progress; developed through Creative Technologies class with Marvin Melzer leading the hardware track.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Parachute Computer</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>The ecosystem umbrella &mdash; the GitHub organization holding the Vault, Daily, and the surrounding coordinated projects.</li>
